==German==

===Etymology===
Related to {{proto|Indo-European|leu-|to detach|lang=de}}. Compare Ancient Greek {{term|sc=polytonic|λύω|tr=luō||loose, untie|lang=grc}}, Latin {{term|solvo|solvō|dissolve|lang=la}}, English {{term|forlorn|lang=en}}.

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|verliert|verlor|verloren}}

# {{transitive}} to [[lose]] (something, or a game)
# {{transitive}} to [[shed]]
# {{reflexive|lang=de}} to [[trail]] [[away]]

